      "footnote_refs": [],
      "footnote_texts": {},
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Law obliges a joint-stock company board member to disclose information regarding that member’s interest in any transaction to be made by the company.   Information regarding an interest in a transaction should be disclosed to the board, and a board member with a conflict of interest in the transaction is deprived of his/her voting right on the approval of that transaction.   [1] In addition, the Law stipulates that the Law's provisions covering joint-stock companies' board members apply to the operations of managers of limited liability companies.   [2]   Therefore, managers of limited liability companies are also obliged to notify the company if they have an interest in any transaction.   As to transactions involving a conflict of interest, the Law does not require that such a transaction be approved by any of the company’s governing bodies either before or after it is made.  ",
